course: dictionary
lesson: 8771
title: Shabbily: worn out and unfair
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Shabbily is an adverb, a describing word that tells you how something is done. It has two meanings, and the context tells you which one fits. «Shabbily dressed» is about how someone looks: their clothes are old, faded and worn.
explain: Shabbily can also describe how someone is treated. To treat someone shabbily is to be unfair or unkind to them, when they deserved better. Ask yourself: is the sentence describing a look, or describing behaviour? That question tells you which meaning to use.
explain: Look at the clue words. In «shabbily dressed men in pot-hats», the word dressed tells you it is about clothes. In «they treated him shabbily», the word treated tells you it is about behaviour. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Shabbily means in a worn-out, old and untidy way, or in an unfair, mean or unkind way.
fact: «Shabbily dressed» means wearing old, faded, worn clothes.
fact: To «treat someone shabbily» means to be unfair to someone who deserved better.
fact: In the example from The Wind in the Willows, «shabbily dressed men in pot-hats» are part of a chasing crowd, and pot-hat means bowler hat.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad escapes from prison dressed in shabby clothes belonging to a washerwoman.
exercise: In «shabbily dressed men in pot-hats», what does shabbily mean? | In smart, expensive clothes | *In old, worn and untidy clothes | Very quickly | In a loud, bright way
exercise: Mia says, «They treated the new boy shabbily.» What does shabbily mean here? | *Unfairly and unkindly | Very slowly | With a big party | Politely, with a smile
exercise: Which word in «shabbily dressed men» tells you the clothes are the thing being described? | men | *dressed | pot-hats | waving
test: «The old room was shabbily furnished, with torn chairs and a cracked table.» What does shabbily mean? | Very brightly lit | In an unfair way to the guests | *In a worn-out, untidy way | Very noisily
test: Ben says the teacher treated the class shabbily when she forgot their trip. Which meaning fits? | *Unfairly, in a way that let the class down | Happily, with a song | Quickly, before lunch | Kindly, with extra treats
exam: Which meaning of shabbily fits «they treated him shabbily» and why? | Bright and shiny, because treated means polished | *Unfair or unkind, because treated is about how someone behaves | Worn-out clothes, because treated is about looks | Very slowly, because treated means taking time
